course: dictionary
lesson: 9182
title: Sob and the feeling behind it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sob is crying that comes in short, sharp, noisy breaths, often with a shaky voice. Read the words around it to see what is happening. «The bird in its cage was sobbing to be let out» tells you the bird is in trouble and wants freedom.
explain: Notice how the sobbing sounds in a story. «Between sobs it all comes out» means the person is crying so hard that they can only speak in small bits, with gaps for breath. The gaps are the clue that the crying is strong.
explain: Sob can also be a noun, a sound you hear. «The Mock Turtle, choking with sobs, sings» shows that sobs are the sounds of loud crying. Some phrases change the meaning too: «sob story» is informal and tells you someone may be making a sad tale sound bigger to get sympathy.
fact: Sob means to cry noisily, with short, sharp breaths.
fact: A sob can also be the sound of loud crying, as in «a sob».
fact: «Sob your heart out» means to cry a lot.
fact: «Sob story» means a sad story told to make people feel sorry for you, maybe to get something.
fact: Sobbing usually shows deep sadness, fear or relief, more than quiet crying does.
exercise: «The bird in its cage was sobbing to be let out.» What does sobbing mean? | Flying around the room | Sleeping quietly | Singing a happy tune | *Crying noisily with short, sharp breaths
exercise: «Between sobs it all comes out.» What does between sobs mean? | *In the short gaps between bursts of crying | After the story has ended | In the middle of a long song | Between two houses on the road
exercise: Find and copy the word that means crying in this sentence: «Toad sobs that he will go out into the dark night.» | share | *sobs | dark | that
test: «Sob story» means: | a true story from history | a story about soup | a funny story for a party | *a sad story told to make people feel sorry for you, maybe to get something
test: Sobbing in a story most often shows: | a good joke | a sleepy yawn | a loud cheer | *deep sadness, fear or relief
exam: Which sentence uses sob as a noun? | *The room was quiet, except for a small sob from the corner. | They sobbed all night long. | The door began to sob. | He will sob until the bus comes.
